# File: tests/blender/test_contract_uv_overlap.py
# Generated from: specs/133-fix-contract-uv-overlap-validation-hanging-for-hours-on-stacked-uvs/requirements.md
Feature: Contract UV overlap validation finishes quickly and reports progress

  @SCN001 @regression
  Scenario: Stacked UVs on a 100k-triangle mesh fail fast
    Given a mesh of at least 100k triangles whose faces all cover the full 0-1 UV square
    And its asset class runs the overlap check
    When contract validation runs on it
    Then a "uv.overlap" finding is reported
    And the overlap check for that mesh finishes within 10 seconds

  @SCN002 @regression
  Scenario: Early exit never changes the overlap outcome
    Given a set of UV faces
    When the overlap fraction is computed
    Then it exceeds OVERLAP_LIMIT exactly when full rasterization of those faces would
    And rasterizing stops once the shared-texel count exceeds OVERLAP_LIMIT times GRID squared

  @SCN003 @regression
  Scenario: An early-exit overlap finding states a lower bound
    Given a mesh where the overlap check stopped early
    When the "uv.overlap" finding is reported
    Then its message says "at least" the reported share of covered UV texels is shared
    And it names the overlap limit

  @SCN004 @regression
  Scenario: A large non-overlapping layout stays fast and passes
    Given a mesh of at least 200k triangles with a non-overlapping UV layout
    When contract validation runs on it
    Then no "uv.overlap" finding is reported
    And the overlap check for that mesh finishes within 30 seconds

  @SCN005 @regression
  Scenario: Existing overlap fixtures keep their results
    Given the existing contract-validate and bake-unique fixtures
    When validation and the bake UV check run on them
    Then each fixture produces the same pass/fail result and finding codes as before

  @SCN006 @regression
  Scenario: The validate step reports per-check progress
    Given a finalize job running the validate step on a collection with several meshes
    When the job status is read during validation
    Then its step is "validate"
    And its progress rises strictly between 0 and 1 as meshes and checks finish
    And its message names the current object and check
